###############################################

# In some cases, you may need to precisely control how your segment 
# instances are mapped out across the hosts in your array. For example, 
# the way gpinitsystem maps segments to segment hosts can change 
# between releases. If you are upgrading using a dump from a prior 
# release to restore into a newer system, use this option to make 
# sure the array layout stays the same as your previous instance. 
# All of the configuration information for an array can be found by 
# looking in the gp_configuration system catalog table.

# Using the -I option with gpinitsystem allows you to supply a 
# detailed array configuration file using the parameters ARRAY_NAME, 
